MoTD javascript
document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', function() {
    // ===== EASILY CONFIGURABLE SETTINGS =====
    const motdConfig = {
        message: "Testing testing 123.....", // Change this text
        backgroundColor: "#FFE4E1" // Light red (mistyrose) - whiteish red as requested
    };
    // ========================================

    // Create MOTD element
    const motd = document.createElement('div');
    motd.textContent = motdConfig.message;
    motd.style.position = 'fixed';
    motd.style.top = '0';
    motd.style.left = '0';
    motd.style.width = '100%';
    motd.style.backgroundColor = motdConfig.backgroundColor;
    motd.style.color = '#333'; // Dark text for readability on light background
    motd.style.textAlign = 'center';
    motd.style.padding = '12px 0';
    motd.style.fontFamily = 'Arial, sans-serif';
    motd.style.fontSize = '16px';
    motd.style.zIndex = '9999';
    motd.style.transition = 'transform 0.2s ease, box-shadow 0.2s ease';
    motd.style.boxShadow = '0 2px 5px rgba(0,0,0,0.1)'; // Subtle shadow for depth
    
    // Add to page (insert after any existing fixed headers)
    document.body.prepend(motd);

    // Hover effect: slight enlargement
    motd.addEventListener('mouseenter', function() {
        this.style.transform = 'scale(1.03)'; // 3% enlargement (tiny bit)
        this.style.boxShadow = '0 4px 8px rgba(0,0,0,0.15)';
    });
    
    motd.addEventListener('mouseleave', function() {
        this.style.transform = 'scale(1)';
        this.style.boxShadow = '0 2px 5px rgba(0,0,0,0.1)';
    });
});
Key features:

Easy Configuration:

Modify motdConfig.message to change the text
Adjust motdConfig.backgroundColor for different shades (currently set to #FFE4E1 - a soft "mistyrose" that meets the "whiteish red" requirement)
Text color (#333) is fixed for optimal readability on the light red background
Hover Effect:

Smooth 3% enlargement on mouse enter (subtle but noticeable)
Returns to normal size on mouse leave
Includes matching shadow adjustment for depth perception
Implementation Notes:

Uses DOMContentLoaded to ensure DOM is ready
Fixed positioning at top (z-index: 9999 ensures it stays above other content)
Includes subtle shadow for visual separation from page content
Responsive width (100% of viewport)
Clean, accessible typography (16px font, proper padding)
To use:

Paste this code into a <script> tag in your HTML (preferably just before </body>)
Or save as motd.js and include with <script src="motd.js"></script>
Simply edit the message and backgroundColor values in the configuration section to customize
Example color variations (all qualify as "whiteish red"):

#FFE4E1 (current - mistyrose)
#FFF0F0 (even lighter)
#FFE6E6 (slightly more red)
#FFD1D1 (more saturated but still light)
The solution maintains performance with CSS transitions and doesn't interfere with existing page functionality while providing a professional, noticeable-yet-unobtrusive notification system.

